---
/** Scoring formats overview page. Ported from react/pages/Scoring.tsx. */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import BackLink from "../../components/BackLink.astro";
---

<Base title="GlideComp - Scoring">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-background text-foreground py-6 px-page-safe">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <header class="mb-10">
        <BackLink href="/" />
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold flex items-center gap-3">
          <img src="/icon.svg" alt="GlideComp logo" class="w-8 h-8" />
          Scoring
        </h1>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1">How GlideComp scores competitions</p>
      </header>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <div class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <p class="text-muted-foreground">
            Every competition is scored in one of two formats, which the organiser picks in the
            competition's settings. The last two guides explain what GlideComp checks and
            repairs in each tracklog before scoring it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* GAP */}
      <a
        href="/scoring/gap"
        class="block mb-6 p-5 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card hover:border-primary/60 transition-colors group"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-2">
          <h2 class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 text-xl font-bold">
            GAP <span class="text-sm font-normal text-muted-foreground">race to goal</span>
          </h2>
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="18"
            height="18"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="shrink-0 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          The FAI/CIVL standard, used at most hang gliding and paragliding competitions. Pilots
          race a set course of turnpoints to goal. A task is worth up to 1000 points, shared out
          for distance, time, leading and arrival according to how each pilot did against the
          rest of the field.
        </p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium mt-3 text-foreground group-hover:underline">
          Read how GAP works
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </a>

      {/* Open Distance */}
      <a
        href="/scoring/open-distance"
        class="block mb-6 p-5 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card hover:border-primary/60 transition-colors group"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-2">
          <h2 class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 text-xl font-bold">
            Open distance
            <span class="text-sm font-normal text-muted-foreground">
              fly as far as you can
            </span>
          </h2>
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="18"
            height="18"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="shrink-0 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          Everyone launches from the same place and flies as far as they can, with no course and
          no goal. Your score is the straight-line distance, in metres, from the edge of the
          take-off cylinder to the furthest point you reached.
        </p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium mt-3 text-foreground group-hover:underline">
          Read how open distance works
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </a>

      {/* Data cleaning */}
      <a
        href="/scoring/data-cleaning"
        class="block mb-6 p-5 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card hover:border-primary/60 transition-colors group"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-2">
          <h2 class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 text-xl font-bold">
            Track data cleaning
            <span class="text-sm font-normal text-muted-foreground">
              honest inputs to honest scores
            </span>
          </h2>
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="18"
            height="18"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="shrink-0 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          GPS dropouts and signal reflections sometimes log an altitude no glider could fly.
          GlideComp repairs these spikes before analysis, by checking the GPS altitude against the
          barometer, or against what a glider can physically do when there is no barometer. The
          pilot's report card lists every repair. Positions, times and the original file are
          never changed.
        </p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium mt-3 text-foreground group-hover:underline">
          Read how data cleaning works
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </a>

      {/* Track validity */}
      <a
        href="/scoring/track-validity"
        class="block mb-6 p-5 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card hover:border-primary/60 transition-colors group"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-2">
          <h2 class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 text-xl font-bold">
            Track validity checks
            <span class="text-sm font-normal text-muted-foreground">
              is this really your flight of this task?
            </span>
          </h2>
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="18"
            height="18"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="shrink-0 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-foreground transition-colors"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          Sometimes a pilot uploads the wrong file, such as a flight from another day or another
          site. GlideComp checks every tracklog against its task, and withholds one that cannot be
          that flight. Lesser concerns are only flagged and never change a score. The scorekeeper
          can overrule any verdict.
        </p>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium mt-3 text-foreground group-hover:underline">
          Read how track validity works
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </a>

      <div class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-border">
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">When the scoring changes</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          When GlideComp fixes a scoring fault or moves closer to the FAI specification, every
          competition is rescored, so your points can change without the organiser doing
          anything. Each change is written up with what moved, who it affects and why.
          <a
            href="https://github.com/pokle/glidecomp/tree/master/web/engine/scoring-changes"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          >
            Read the scoring changelog on GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
